cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fortran_cubatures: Gaussian cubature rules for finite elements"
type: software
abstract: >-
  fortran_cubatures is a Fortran module, cubatures, with the derived type
  cubature: the abscissae and weights of a Gaussian integration rule on one of
  the six reference elements of the finite element method (line, triangle,
  quadrilateral, tetrahedron, hexahedron and wedge). Rules are selected by
  degree of exactness, for any degree, with separate degrees per direction on
  tensor-product elements. Triangles and tetrahedra use tabulated symmetric
  rules at low degree and collapsed Gauss-Jacobi rules above. Every rule has
  positive weights and interior points and is checked by monomial-exactness
  tests. It is Fortran 2018 and builds with fpm or make.
authors:
